  "meta": {
    "title": "aⁱbʲcᵏ with i × j = k — multiplication checked in place",
    "blurb": "Sipser’s M₃ as a linear bounded automaton. Check the shape, then for every a, cross off one c for every b. When the a’s run out, every c must be crossed off. Multiplication as repeated addition, never leaving the input’s cells.",
    "inputs": [
      {
        "w": "abc",
        "expect": "accept",
        "label": "1 × 1 = 1"
      },
      {
        "w": "abbcc",
        "expect": "accept",
        "label": "1 × 2 = 2"
      },
      {
        "w": "aabcc",
        "expect": "accept",
        "label": "2 × 1 = 2"
      },
      {
        "w": "aabbcccc",
        "expect": "accept",
        "label": "2 × 2 = 4"
      },
      {
        "w": "aaabbcccccc",
        "expect": "accept",
        "label": "3 × 2 = 6"
      },
      {
        "w": "abbc",
        "expect": "reject",
        "label": "1 × 2 ≠ 1"
      },
      {
        "w": "aabbccc",
        "expect": "reject",
        "label": "2 × 2 ≠ 3"
      },
      {
        "w": "bc",
        "expect": "reject",
        "label": "no a"
      },
      {
        "w": "abcabc",
        "expect": "reject"
      }
    ],
    "library": {
      "author": {
        "login": "thethinkmachine"
      },
      "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
      "tags": [
        "sipser",
        "arithmetic",
        "context-sensitive",
        "not-context-free"
      ],
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "chapter": "Sipser, Introduction to the Theory of Computation, Example 3.11",
      "readme": "Sipser gives M₃ as a four-stage description; this is it with every state drawn.\n\n1. **Shape.** The first four states check the input is a⁺b⁺c⁺ and nothing else.\n2. **Rewind** to the ⊢ endmarker.\n3. **One round per a.** *next a* crosses off an a (A). Then *find b* / *find c* / *back to b* pair each b with a c, marking them B and C. When no unmarked b remains (*find b* meets a C), *restore b* turns the B's back into b's for the next round.\n4. When *next a* finds no a left, *all c crossed?* checks the rest of the tape.\n\nAfter i rounds, i × j c's are crossed off; a round that runs out of c's gets stuck and rejects. Nothing is ever written outside the input, which is what makes it a **linear bounded automaton** — the machine model of the context-sensitive languages. The language is not context-free."
    }
  }
}
